<div class="WordSection1">Hi,<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas Freight.<br />
<br />
If you would like to enquire about adding excess baggage to your flight, you’ll need to visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/baggage/additional-baggage.html">Qantas Passenger’s website</a> or call them on <b>13 13 13</b>.<br />
<br />
If you have a passport and intended proof of travel (a boarding pass or e-ticket) you may be eligible to use our unaccompanied baggage service via Qantas Freight. Keep in mind you will need to allow approximately 10 days for shipment to move and are terminal fees up to $150.00 plus the freight weight cost.<br />
<br />
We offer this service from some of our major international freight terminals in Australia (excluding Brisbane).<br />
<br />
Unaccompanied baggage must meet the following criteria:<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;It is personal goods such as clothing, books, musical instruments or sporting equipment<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Each bag must not weigh more than 32kgs – however there is no limit on total weight<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;All packaging of bags and boxes must be complete before you lodge your baggage<br />
<br />
All domestic unaccompanied baggage quotes are generated online <a href="https://freight.qantas.com/quote-book.html">here</a>.<br />
<br />
For a quote for international unaccompanied baggage, simply reply to this email or call <b>13 12 13</b> with the following details:<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Origin and destination<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Length, width and height (cm) of each piece<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Weight (kg)<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Description</div>
